 "/athletes/69728"} "Ilona Slupianek"] " (GDR) who broke the world record twice in May with 22.36 (73-4½) and 22.45 (73-8). Slupianek won the gold medal in round one with 22.41 (73-6¼) and dominated the competition. Her worst mark of six fair throws was 21.42 (70-3½), which would have tied for the silver medal. The silver medalist was " [:a {:href "/athletes/77184"} "Esfir Krachevskaya"] ", who had competed in 1972 as Esfir Dolzhenko. Slupianek had not competed in 1979, having tested positive for steroids, and she has the infamy of being the first East German to fail a doping test."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Start Order"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Distance"] [:th {} "Round #1 Distance"] [:th {} "Round #2 Distance"] [:th {} "Round #3 Distance"] [:th {} "Round #4 Distance"] [:th {} "Round #5 Distance"] [:th {} "Round #6 Distance"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "136"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/69728"} "Ilona Slupianek"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "22.41"] [:td {} "22.41"] [:td {} "21.81"] [:td {} "21.42"] [:td {} "21.60"] [:td {} "22.00"] [:td {} "21.85"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "Olympic Record"} "OR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "272"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/77184"} "Esfir Krachevskaya"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/URS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/URS.png"}] "URS"]] [:td {} "21.42"] [:td {} "20.00"] [:td {} "20.67"] [:td {} "21.42"] [:td {} "x"] [:td {} "21.03"] [:td {} "x"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}